hi i'm kendra hutchins manager of the  cornell annual trials program  i've run the program for five years now  and we've never had a year quite like  this one  cobit 19 wasn't even an issue when i  started sewing seed this spring  but then cornell closed down in march we  got permission to continue  our trials but it was a bare bones  operation co-workers pitched in to help  with transplanting  masked and socially distanced of course  with their help  we managed to get thousands of plants in  the ground 185 cultivars from eight  companies it was a hot dry season  but our new drip irrigation system  helped to keep everything looking good  sadly we had to cancel our field day but  we've continued evaluating cultivars  at the end of the season we'll post a  list of our top performers on our  website  where you can also find more information  about our program  until then follow our progress on  facebook and instagram  thanks for watching and stay safe this  has been a production  of cornell university
 

